{
  "_why": "The hand-built demo rigs, and WHY THEY ARE NOT ON SLOTS 0-11 ANY MORE. They used to sit on 0-11, which is where the FM3 keeps 59 Bassguy, 65 Bassguy, Vibrato Lux and nine more real factory presets — so the one unit with hand-built content was the one unit whose factory bank you could not check against the thing on your desk. \"With the FM3, they are not the actual default presets. One of them says Papa’s Roach, which definitely is not a preset that should be in the demo. It should have the real factory presets like all the others do.\" The FM3 bank is 384 entries, 0-383, so these start at 384 — which on a real FM3 is where a player’s own presets go. Nothing is lost: the Edit screen still has twelve rigs with real models and named scenes to demonstrate, and every factory slot now reads the way the unit does.",
